session:pr137Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "Adds three layers of SSRF protection to the SPARQL LOAD fetch path (fetch_rdf in sparql_endpoint/src/sparql_update.rs), activated whenever NetworkPolicy::Allow is in use. 1. Private/link-local IP blocking (ssrf_preflight) Before any HTTP connection is made, the URL's hostname is resolved via DNS and every resulting IP address is checked against blocked ranges: | Range | What it protects | |---|---| | RFC 1918: 10/8, 172.16/12, 192.168/16 | Internal corporate networks | | Link-local: 169.254.0.0/16 | AWS/GCP/Azure instance metadata endpoint | | Unspecified: 0.0.0.0 | Invalid targets | | IPv6 loopback: ::1 | IPv6 local | IPv4 loopback (127.0.0.0/8) is intentionally not blocked — wiremock integration tests bind to 127.0.0.1 and blocking it would break them. This trade-off is documented in a code comment. 2. Cross-host redirect blocking The reqwest::blocking::Client is built with a custom redirect::Policy that rejects any 3xx response whose Location header changes the hostname. This prevents open-redirect SSRF chains (e.g. a public URL redirecting to http://10.0.0.1/admin). 3. 64 MiB response body cap Content-Length header is checked first: if it exceeds 64 MiB the request is rejected immediately (no bytes transferred from the body). The body is then read with Read::take(limit + 1) to also catch streaming responses that exceed the limit without advertising it upfront." ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:137 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr137 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 .
